{"id":5072,"date":"2021-09-01T12:11:12","date_gmt":"2021-09-01T12:11:12","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?p=5072"},"modified":"2021-09-14T12:25:06","modified_gmt":"2021-09-14T12:25:06","slug":"excitement-as-aims-ghana-receives-over-40-young-africans","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/excitement-as-aims-ghana-receives-over-40-young-africans\/","title":{"rendered":"Excitement as AIMS Ghana receives over 50 young Africans!"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>The new 2021-2022 cohort has officially started at AIMS Ghana, with over 50 young Africans arriving from more than 15 African nations! Though lectures have already begun, the first week is also used to orient students, where they meet with staff and get to familiarize themselves with their colleagues. According to them, it has been very exciting so far. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>&#8220;The AIMS training will equip you with academic, technical, and soft skills which will help you tackle the world&#8217;s challenges upon graduation,&#8221; said the AIMS Ghana Centre President, Dr. Prince Osei. &#8220;If you utilize the networking opportunities that AIMS presents you, it will open a lot of doors for you.&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The AIMS Ghana COO, Ms. Adelaide Asante also led the opening presentation where the students were introduced to all the activities that are run at the Centre.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We are confident that with the student talents and abilities, together with hard work, dedication and passion, they will contribute enormously to the growth and development of Africa.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-1 wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/09\/2022-1024x683.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5073\" data-full-url=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads